        {
          "question": "q-325128",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}={y}^{3}-x,\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $\u0394x=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055697/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "f50e2158d16f3e430188beee745393be38c085ecb8209494f1baa57ec0cd1b56"
