      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21317",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny' = y^3 - x\\,y, \\qquad y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $\\Delta x = 1,$ the new value $y_\\text{new}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g(y_\\text{new}) = 0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **specific function** $g(y_\\text{new})$ used in the first step?\n\n- $g(y_\\text{new}) = (y_\\text{new})^3 - 3y_\\text{new} - 1$\n\n- $g(y_\\text{new}) = 3y_\\text{new} - (y_\\text{new})^3 + 1$\n\n- $g(y_\\text{new}) = 3y_\\text{new} - (y_\\text{new})^3 - 1$\n\n- $g(y_\\text{new}) = y_\\text{new} - (y_\\text{new})^3 + x_\\text{new}y_\\text{new}$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055697/example-21317.json",
          "file_sha256": "accf7a352b6c6b3aac97e871af52037f83541c9b771bb8ac5acc798befc68fdf"
        }
      ],
