    {
      "question": "e-21317",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "a684ca3f6de257e322302ca3f844cf6e6d93109efb565c5cc5c1a869da56e574",
      "new_sha256": "13ef9ebaefefd5e4c3abc2440eca58596303f50473b0e5da0484d9d9aeb269ba",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21317",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y_0 = y(x_0),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = y'_\\text{new} \\cdot \\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwith $y'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new},y_\\text{new})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $\\Delta y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & =({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into $y_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g(y_\\text{new}){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\u0394y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {{{y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y}_{\u23df}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $\\Delta x = 1$ is\n\n$$\ng(y_\\text{new}) = y_\\text{new} - (y_\\text{new})^3 + x_\\text{new}y_\\text{new} - y.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is $x_\\text{new} = x + \\Delta x = 1 + 1 = 2.$ Therefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+2{y}_{\\text{new}}-1 \\\\  & =3{y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055697/example-21317.json",
          "file_sha256": "accf7a352b6c6b3aac97e871af52037f83541c9b771bb8ac5acc798befc68fdf"
        }
      ],
